From: Mike Ward <mward5@tinfoil-fedora.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hi556: report camera orientation and rotation

hi556 never calls v4l2_fwnode_device_parse() /
v4l2_ctrl_new_fwnode_properties(), so it exposes neither
V4L2_CID_CAMERA_ORIENTATION nor V4L2_CID_CAMERA_SENSOR_ROTATION even
when the platform describes them.

On ACPI platforms the information is already available and already
parsed: ipu-bridge reads the panel position from _PLD and the rotation
from the SSDB, and attaches both to the sensor's software node as the
"orientation" and "rotation" properties. Without the corresponding
controls the sensor driver simply drops them, and userspace has no way
to tell where the camera is pointing.

The visible effect is that libcamera cannot populate
properties::Location, and falls back to naming the camera after its
model. On a Dell XPS 13 9315 2-in-1 the internal front camera is
reported as "hi556" while the back camera, whose driver does report
orientation, is correctly reported as "Internal back camera".
libcamera flags the omission explicitly at probe time:

  'hi556 0-0020': Recommended V4L2 control 0x009a0922 not supported
  'hi556 0-0020': The sensor kernel driver needs to be fixed
  'hi556 0-0020': Failed to retrieve the camera location
  'hi556 0-0020': Rotation control not available, default to 0 degrees

Parse the fwnode properties and register the corresponding controls,
as most other sensor drivers already do. Verified on the machine above,
where _PLD reports panel 4 (front) for the hi556 and panel 5 (back) for
the rear sensor.

Signed-off-by: Mike Ward <mward5@tinfoil-fedora.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
index 0dae0438aa80..1111111111111 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
@@ -847,12 +847,13 @@ static const struct v4l2_ctrl_ops hi556_ctrl_ops = {

 static int hi556_init_controls(struct hi556 *hi556)
 {
+	struct v4l2_fwnode_device_properties props;
 	struct v4l2_ctrl_handler *ctrl_hdlr;
 	s64 exposure_max, h_blank;
 	int ret;

 	ctrl_hdlr = &hi556->ctrl_handler;
-	ret = v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(ctrl_hdlr, 8);
+	ret = v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(ctrl_hdlr, 10);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

@@ -906,6 +907,17 @@ static int hi556_init_controls(struct hi556 *hi556)
 	if (ctrl_hdlr->error)
 		return ctrl_hdlr->error;

+	ret = v4l2_fwnode_device_parse(hi556->dev, &props);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = v4l2_ctrl_new_fwnode_properties(ctrl_hdlr, &hi556_ctrl_ops,
+					      &props);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (ctrl_hdlr->error)
+		return ctrl_hdlr->error;
+
 	hi556->sd.ctrl_handler = ctrl_hdlr;

 	return 0;
